From b4df8d3ab323947ce84cc5e33403f78377b6921b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:37:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06907/11362] [outer-loop] sk48: L3 SOLVED round 7 (codex,
 ordering strip decoded)

Round-7 gpt-5.6-sol session mapped the exact win condition six prior
rounds' honest-null attempts were missing: the horizontal ordering
strip requires the head-to-tail color sequence 8 -> 12 -> 9 -> 14
(read from the bottom head outward), NOT the vertical rack's
top-to-bottom order (14 -> 9 -> 8 -> 12), which looks deceptively
similar. L3 is sequence-sensitive: blocks must be staged via
alternating vertical carries and horizontal retract/extend transfers
so the active chain accumulates the target prefixes in order. A
detached block only follows horizontal retraction correctly after
first being threaded while pinned to the perpendicular vertical chain.

Winning line: 37-action L3 tail after the banked 44-action L1-L2
prefix (81 actions total). The source agent's own fresh-environment
reproduction gate confirmed reached_level=3. The outer loop
independently re-verified regardless: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay
via a new resolver priority branch, all 5 confirmed level=3,
state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED.

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: sk48 levels_reproduced 2 -> 3.
reproducible_total_levels 163 -> 164 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
